From c641a0aea65316535729a52eecd9ac24f7bd73e9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kartikya Motwani <kartikya@local>
Date: Wed, 26 Aug 2026 19:51:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix Total Return showing a bogus instant gain on every bot
 restart

Reported today: Dashboard showed "Total Return: +19.06% since
inception" and a matching "+Rs.19,064" the instant the bot was
restarted - even though the equity curve chart (built from real
PortfolioSnapshot history) was visibly trending DOWN, not up. A clear
contradiction between the chart and the summary card.

Root cause: self.starting_capital (used by status() to compute
total_return_pct and day_pnl) was always reset fresh to whatever got
passed to start() - typically settings.PAPER_STARTING_CAPITAL
(Rs.100,000) or the Live Bot form's "Starting Capital" field default -
every single time the bot started, completely disconnected from
broker.cash/positions, which DO correctly resume real history via
_restore_state() (fixed in an earlier session). So total_return_pct
was computing (real resumed portfolio value - a fake reset baseline)
every restart, producing a bogus "instant profit" that had nothing to
do with actual performance - it was purely an artifact of comparing
a real number against the wrong baseline.

Fix: start() now looks up the very first-ever BotSession for this
user_id (ordered by started_at ascending) and uses ITS
starting_capital as the permanent "since inception" baseline,
regardless of what gets passed to this particular start() call. A
genuinely brand-new user (no prior session) still starts fresh with
whatever capital they specify, unchanged. The new BotSession DB row
still records this session's own nominal starting_capital as before
(informational per-session record) - only the in-memory
self.starting_capital used for return calculations now reflects the
true inception baseline.

Verified end-to-end with an in-memory test DB: session 1 establishes
a Rs.100,000 baseline; session 2 (simulating a restart) passes a
deliberately different Rs.250,000 but correctly ends up with
self.starting_capital == 100,000 (the true first-session baseline),
not 250,000. Separately verified a genuinely new user_id with no
prior sessions still starts fresh with whatever capital they specify.
All 17 existing tests still pass.
---
 app/bot_runner.py | 22 ++++++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 20 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/app/bot_runner.py b/app/bot_runner.py
index 3657ac9..913d5f3 100644
--- a/app/bot_runner.py
+++ b/app/bot_runner.py
@@ -126,13 +126,31 @@ class BotRunner:
             return {"status": False, "reason": f"unknown_strategy: {strategy_name}"}
 
         symbols = symbols or list(DEFAULT_WATCHLIST.keys())
+        session_starting_capital = starting_capital if starting_capital is not None else settings.PAPER_STARTING_CAPITAL
 
         db = SessionLocal()
+
+        # The TRUE "since inception" baseline is the very first session this
+        # user ever ran, not whatever gets passed to this particular
+        # start() call. broker.cash/positions already correctly resume
+        # across restarts (_restore_state()) - but self.starting_capital
+        # was always reset fresh here, so total_return_pct in status() was
+        # comparing the real resumed portfolio value against a fake reset
+        # baseline every time, producing a bogus "instant profit" on every
+        # restart that had nothing to do with actual performance.
+        first_session = (
+            db.query(BotSession)
+            .filter(BotSession.user_id == self.user_id)
+            .order_by(BotSession.started_at.asc())
+            .first()
+        )
+        inception_starting_capital = first_session.starting_capital if first_session else session_starting_capital
+
         bot_session = BotSession(
             started_at=datetime.utcnow(),
             symbol=",".join(symbols),
             strategy_name=strategy_name,
-            starting_capital=starting_capital if starting_capital is not None else settings.PAPER_STARTING_CAPITAL,
+            starting_capital=session_starting_capital,
             is_live=(settings.MODE == "live"),
             status="running",
             user_id=self.user_id,
@@ -148,7 +166,7 @@ class BotRunner:
         self.strategies = {sym: strategy_cls() for sym in symbols}
         self.tick_seconds = tick_seconds
         self.last_signal = {sym: "HOLD" for sym in symbols}
-        self.starting_capital = starting_capital if starting_capital is not None else settings.PAPER_STARTING_CAPITAL
+        self.starting_capital = inception_starting_capital
         self.running = True
 
         self.thread = threading.Thread(target=self._run_loop, daemon=True)
